/*
 * Where the parser was when it found an error, which tells
 * `Parser.synchronize` where reading can safely start again:
 *
 * - `File`: between declarations of the file, so the next `proc`,
 *   `class`, `use` or other declaration;
 * - `Member`: inside a class, struct or interface, so the next
 *   `public`, `proc`, `@` or the `}` that closes it;
 * - `Statement`: inside a block, so the next statement or the `}`
 *   that closes the block.
 *
 * In every scope a `;` or the start of a new line is also a safe place,
 * except while skipping the body of a malformed member.
 *
 * @since 0.8
 * @author Edynu
 */

public enum SyncScope {
    File,
    Member,
    Statement
}